 "notes": "Own row has no pool, pit or grave; first publication (Dever 1973a) not accessed. No survey entry. SWP: Balata (II p. 156) is this unit; its only candidate is Joseph's tomb, said to be close to Balanus, no direction (position none, type not stated). 'Askar (II p. 156) describes 'Askar (S825, 820 m): its sepulchres given S825's point (E84 'Askar lies at another point). Mohnah, 'Asiret el Kibliyeh/Beit Iba, Beth Bezzin, Sebustieh, Sozura/'Ain Beit Ilma, El Wiria and El Mugheir are other places, not shown within 2 km; ignored. S825/E90 'late Rom' mausoleum coded L (late Roman after 135 CE). S826 soldiers' tombstones not coded as graves. E92 coordinates approximate per its comment."
